# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Watchtower is the PUBLIC, sanitized mirror of a private engineering knowledge
# base. The folders below exist here only as structural stubs: their skeleton is
# tracked (via .gitkeep) so the shape of the system is legible, but their content
# is deliberately withheld and must never be committed to this public repo.
#
# Pattern: ignore everything inside the folder, then re-include its .gitkeep.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Security: DOCTRINE ships (the layer model, the IR template); POSTURE does not.
# A page describing which controls a running system has is also a page describing
# which it lacks, and genericizing the names does not change that. Keep filled-in
# copies, and the risk register, in a private clone.
/wiki/security/*
!/wiki/security/_index.md
!/wiki/security/defense-in-depth-model.md
!/wiki/security/incident-response-template.md

# Withheld: product roadmaps (incl. client-owned apps)
/wiki/roadmaps/*
!/wiki/roadmaps/.gitkeep

# Withheld: per-project business/operational pages
/wiki/projects/*
!/wiki/projects/.gitkeep

# Withheld: dated internal churn logs (PR numbers, rollout status)
/wiki/logs/*
!/wiki/logs/.gitkeep

# Withheld: internal todo backlogs
/wiki/todos/*
!/wiki/todos/.gitkeep

# Withheld: internal infrastructure topology (hosts, cluster, deploy plumbing)
/wiki/infra/*
!/wiki/infra/.gitkeep

# Withheld: work-in-progress session snapshots (reference private internals)
/saves/*
!/saves/.gitkeep

# Withheld: generated audit/scan reports
/reports/*
!/reports/.gitkeep

# Withheld: long-form internal planning content
/content/*
!/content/.gitkeep

# ── Editor / OS / language cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/.idea/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
.env
